t but when you dox  supreme court justices and you publish  wide and large their addresses you leave  them open to potential danger here yeah  democrats are playing with fire here  when they refuse to unequivocally  condemn this pressure campaign at the  supreme court justice's own homes their  personal homes  in an attempt to pressure their decision  making on this upcoming case and keep in  mind the decision has not been made and  federal law is pretty clear that any  such you know harassment or or just uh  undue pressure on judges in particular  is against the law and i've been stunned  that you know you haven't seen clearer  rhetoric from joe biden from the white  house from gensake this is a  the democrats could get some political  attraction in in defending abortion  rights but they can't do it when they  sound extreme or they're defending the  most extreme elements within their own  base yeah on the subject of extreme a  lot of republicans bill as we switch  gears think that this disinformation  governance board is extreme they're  trying to take measures to prevent  funding it lauren bobert the republican  representative from colorado said i  don't think people are fully  understanding the severity of what a  ministry of truth organized by dhs truly  means this is stalin level this is mao  level this is the hill to die on  is it the hill to die on bill  well you know first of all it's entirely  inappropriate in a free country to have  something like this but you would think  this thing would be thrown out  immediately on the basis the fact that  the woman is being recommended to head  the  ministry of disinformation has been  wrong on everything  she got everything wrong she disinformed  on hunter biden she disinformed on  russian collusion and so on  this is another big fat target  democrats have presented for themselves  a real mistake we don't need it we don't  want it  and god knows i think we'll be spared it  of course we all know now we're very  familiar with that mary poppins video  that nina jankowicz did but we also have  a new tweet that has come to light via  the washington examiner in which he said  on november the 1st 2020 trump had not  won but two secret email servers to  communicate with an influential russian  bank unbelievable  katie that's disinformation  yeah that is disinformation and this is  not the only corner of the  administration where this disinformation  is coming from the incoming white house  press secretary uh karine gene pierre  also said that the georgia election was  stolen from stacey abrams and that  president trump wasn't a legitimate  president so there is this very serious  question about the biden administration  creating this new board not to you know  serve as a way to tamp down on  disinformation which used to be a term  that was reserved for homeland security  dealing with outside foreign influence  and information inside the united states  but to go after political enemies inside  the country without any recourse because  they're not elected and it's very  difficult to get through the bureaucracy  and understand what they're doing and i  would note that the dhs secretary can't  define what the mission is of the board  and therefore it's right for abuse i  wanted to ask josh about that in the 45  seconds we've got last the fact that  alejandro mayorkas knew so little about  all of this what does that say to you  not an encouraging sign john that  it doesn't seem like they vetted the the  per nina jankowicz the person who who is  going to be heading this disinformation  uh committee uh i mean and i i i if you  can't vet your own staff and you don't  see this stuff uh that that's clearly  been out there now for the last week  it's a real big red flag i would expect  that if republicans take back the house  uh in in november the if it still exists  by by 2023 there's going to be a lot of  oversight and it's not going to last  much longer all right well i assume that  they know 